# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Tooling caches
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.tox/
.coverage
htmlcov/
.python-version
*.log

# Environment / secrets
.env
.env.*
*.env

# Editors and OS cruft
.idea/
.vscode/
.claude/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Downloaded media and yt-dlp intermediates. These land in the working
# directory whenever the tool is run with `-o .`. Anchored with a leading "/"
# so the patterns only cover the repository root - an unanchored *.mp4 would
# also swallow a deliberate test fixture under tests/.
/*.part
# Fragment temporaries are named "<file>.part-FragN", which does not end in
# ".part" and so is not covered by the pattern above.
/*.part-Frag*
/*.ytdl
/*.mp4
/*.mkv
/*.webm
/*.mp3
/*.m4a
/*.opus
# Containers the no-ffmpeg single-file path can hand back.
/*.m4v
/*.3gp
/*.flv
/*.ogg
/*.aac
/*.wav
# Subtitle formats. --subtitles asks for the best available, which is usually
# vtt, but YouTube offers the others and yt-dlp will write whichever it gets.
/*.vtt
/*.srt
/*.ass
/*.ttml
/*.json3
/*.srv[123]

# Pre-publication audit report. A working document, not a project deliverable -
# and this repository is already public, so committing it would publish an
# audit naming defects that are still open. Kept under tests/ with the rest of
# the working files, so the entries are anchored there.
/tests/AUDIT_FINDINGS.md
/tests/FINDINGS.md
# The session log is the same class of document: an internal record of what was
# changed and why, written in terms of the audit's own finding numbers. It
# cross-references FINDINGS.md, which is excluded above, so published on its own
# every one of those references would dangle.
/tests/LOG.md
# The verification report is written in the same finding numbers and against
# the same two files, so it is excluded for the same reason.
/tests/VERIFY.md
